# Reflection on Professional Networking Assessment

## Situation
I completed an assessment on the fundamentals of professional networking. 
The quiz tested my understanding of the primary purpose of networking, the "golden rule" of networking, and common mistakes to avoid when building professional relationships.

## Task
The task was to demonstrate that I comprehend networking as a strategic, long-term process for building mutually beneficial relationships, rather than simply asking for a job. 
  I needed to show that I understand the etiquette and mindset required to network effectively.

## Action
I reviewed the course content on networking, focusing on the idea that networking is about giving value before asking for anything in return. 
I reflected on the "golden rule" of networking—building genuine connections based on trust and reciprocity. 
I also considered the common pitfalls, such as being too transactional or failing to follow up after meeting someone, and made a mental note to avoid them in my own practice.

## Result
I achieved a 100% score on the assessment. This result confirmed that I have a solid foundation in professional networking principles. 
I now understand that the first step in creating a network is to identify my goals and then reach out to people who can help me achieve them, 
while always offering something of value in return. 
I am ready to start building my professional network with confidence and authenticity.
